WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.160
Hey guys, Dr. Berg here.

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:05.839
In this short video we're going to show you
two different simple home tests that you can

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:06.920
do for adrenal fatigue.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.830
All you need is a flashlight.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.889
Number one, the holding your breath test.

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:16.730
Now one good indication of adrenal fatigue
is the ability to hold your breath for long

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:17.730
periods of time.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:23.970
If you can't, you probably have an adrenal
issue, because the oxygen in your lungs is

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:30.460
connected to the adrenals, and so if you have
really good adrenals you can hold your breath

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.550
for like a minute or longer.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.390
There's a guy who came to my office who is
80 years old.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.760
He had the best adrenals I've ever seen in
my life.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.780
He can heal real fast and I have a machine
that measures the adrenals and he had a perfect

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:43.780
score.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.899
I asked him, "What did he do his whole life?"

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:56.370
Well, he took first place in the Olympics
when he was like 20 years old for water polo,

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:01.440
and he was able to hold his breath for at
least three to four minutes, so he can actually

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.830
hold his breath now for three minutes underneath
the water, so his adrenals are really tough.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.970
You have adrenal case, they're huffing and
puffing.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.380
Up stairs, they run out of air real quick.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.470
They cannot hold their breath.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.860
That's the first test.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.110
Number two is the iris test.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.110
Now what is the iris?

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.360
The iris is kind of like the aperture of the
eye.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.440
Now what is an aperture?

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.740
Aperture is just a opening in the camera that
allows the light to go in at a certain level,

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.310
so this is the same thing.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:35.030
If there's a real bright light, the iris contracts
and constricts the amount of light going into

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.060
the eye because it might be too harmful.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.000
If it's dark out it actually is very, very
open.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.490
It controls the light.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:50.580
If I'm going to shine a light into the eye
like this, this thing normally should contract.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:55.200
Now what's controlling that is something called
the autonomic nervous system or the sympathetic

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.640
nervous system.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.640
What is that?

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.970
That's part of the nervous system that is
intimately involved with flight or fight and

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.110
the adrenal.

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:05.810
The adrenals control that.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.899
Other parts of the body control it, but the
adrenal gland is also involved, so if there's

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:15.020
a weakness with the adrenal and you shine
a light into the eye, what'll happen, it'll

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:19.530
contract, it'll constrict, but it will not
maintain that constriction, so it might kind

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:25.600
of hold it for about five seconds or ten seconds
and it starts going ... It actually fluctuates.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:32.730
It kind of comes open and close because it
cannot hold that constriction.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:38.120
If you can hold that constriction and keep
this thing constricted for at least a minute,

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.120
then your adrenals are good, so it's a real
simple test.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.730
In this next part I'll show you exactly how
to do a little demo of how to do it.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.610
Okay guys, the first thing we're going to
do is we're going to shine a light into the

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:53.780
eye, and if you see the little black part
in the center, that's the pupil.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:58.230
That's the hole right into the eye, and then
the other part, which is kind of the colored

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.819
part, that's called the iris.

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:03.480
That's contracting, constricting, and relaxing.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:10.290
When that contracts it makes the pupil, the
little center part, get smaller or larger,

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.640
depending on what's happening.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:18.470
When you shine light in there, normally the
iris, the outer part, is supposed to contract

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:23.240
and hold that position for at least one to
two minutes.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:30.390
If that contraction cannot occur, that means
the adrenal glands are weak, and you'll start

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:36.910
seeing the pupil get bigger and small like
a wave, like it will not be able to maintain

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:40.820
the very tight contraction.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.840
You just do this in the mirror.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.480
Look into the mirror, shine the light into
the eye.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:51.740
The small little pupil should get smaller
and maintain that smallness by keeping the

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.170
light held steady.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:57.500
If it starts to get weak and start to open
up, which a lot of times it will within about,

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:03.030
I don't know, 10-15 seconds, then we know
the adrenals are weak because the entire nervous

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.270
system that controls that is weak.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:09.420
Okay guys, so now that you have a way to figure
out your adrenals then the question is what

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.020
do you do about it?

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:15.569
There's a great little kit that I have to
help the adrenal glands.

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:16.910
I put the link below.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.280
Check it out if you want some help.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:18.930
Thanks for watching.

